@startuml

title 12.6. Order and purchase UI status cycle completion

hide circle
skinparam linetype ortho

component "OrderController" as OrderController <<implemented>>
component "PurchaseController" as PurchaseController <<implemented>>
component "InventoryDocumentController" as InventoryDocumentController <<partial>>
component "OrderWorkflowDefinition" as OrderWorkflowDefinition <<implemented>>
component "PurchaseWorkflowDefinition" as PurchaseWorkflowDefinition <<implemented>>
component "InventoryPostingService" as InventoryPostingService <<implemented>>
component "DocumentProgressRecalculator" as DocumentProgressRecalculator <<implemented>>
component "BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer" as BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer <<implemented>>
component "PurchaseReceiptUseCase" as PurchaseReceiptUseCase <<implemented>>
component "OrderShipmentUseCase" as OrderShipmentUseCase <<implemented>>

package "Executable from current UI" as CurrentUi {
	[Order: draft -> confirmed]
	[Order: confirmed -> draft]
	[Order: shipped -> delivered]
	[Order: delivered -> completed]
	[Order: not completed/canceled -> canceled]
	[Purchase: draft -> ordered]
	[Purchase: ordered -> draft]
	[Purchase: draft/ordered -> canceled]
	[Purchase: received -> completed]
	[InventoryDocument: draft -> posted]
	[InventoryDocument: draft/posted -> canceled]
}

package "Not executable as a full commercial document cycle" as MissingUi {
	[12.6.1 Purchase receipt UI action] <<implemented>>
	[12.6.2 Order shipment UI action] <<implemented>>
	[12.6.3 Immediate order readiness sync after confirm] <<implemented>>
	[12.6.4 Linked inventory document navigation and audit tests] <<implemented>>
}

package "Derived status source of truth" as Derived {
	[Purchase: partially_received/received]
	[Purchase: partially_returned/returned]
	[Order: awaiting_stock/ready_to_ship]
	[Order: partially_shipped/shipped]
	[Order: partially_returned/returned]
}

OrderController --> [Order: draft -> confirmed]
OrderController --> [Order: confirmed -> draft]
OrderController --> [Order: shipped -> delivered]
OrderController --> [Order: delivered -> completed]
OrderController --> [Order: not completed/canceled -> canceled]
PurchaseController --> [Purchase: draft -> ordered]
PurchaseController --> [Purchase: ordered -> draft]
PurchaseController --> [Purchase: draft/ordered -> canceled]
PurchaseController --> [Purchase: received -> completed]
InventoryDocumentController --> [InventoryDocument: draft -> posted]
InventoryDocumentController --> [InventoryDocument: draft/posted -> canceled]

OrderWorkflowDefinition --> OrderController
PurchaseWorkflowDefinition --> PurchaseController
InventoryPostingService --> InventoryDocumentController
InventoryPostingService --> DocumentProgressRecalculator
DocumentProgressRecalculator --> BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer
BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer --> Derived
PurchaseReceiptUseCase --> [12.6.1 Purchase receipt UI action]
OrderShipmentUseCase --> [12.6.2 Order shipment UI action]

[Purchase: partially_received/received] --> [12.6.1 Purchase receipt UI action]
[Order: partially_shipped/shipped] --> [12.6.2 Order shipment UI action]
[Order: awaiting_stock/ready_to_ship] --> [12.6.3 Immediate order readiness sync after confirm]
[InventoryDocument: draft -> posted] --> [12.6.4 Linked inventory document navigation and audit tests]

note right of CurrentUi
  Audit result from current controllers/templates:

  Order show card can execute:
  - draft -> confirmed;
  - confirmed -> draft;
  - shipped -> delivered;
  - delivered -> completed;
  - cancel while not completed/canceled.

  Purchase show card can execute:
  - draft -> ordered;
  - ordered -> draft;
  - draft/ordered -> canceled;
  - received -> completed.

  Inventory document show card can execute:
  - draft -> posted;
  - draft/posted -> canceled.

  These actions are covered by controllers and CSRF-protected forms,
  but they do not create purchase receipts or order shipments.
end note

note right of Derived
  Required model rule:

  Do not set these statuses directly from a UI button:
  - purchase received/shipping-return states;
  - order stock readiness/shipment-return states.

  They are derived from posted InventoryDocumentLine rows by:
  - InventoryPostingService;
  - DocumentProgressRecalculator;
  - BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer.

  Therefore the missing UI must create/post the correct linked
  inventory documents instead of overwriting PurchaseStatus or
  OrderStatus manually.
end note

note right of [12.6.1 Purchase receipt UI action]
  Goal:
  Make purchase ordered/partially_received -> received executable
  from the purchase UI.

  Implemented:
  1. Added PurchaseReceiptUseCase in the business/service layer.
  2. It builds a draft InventoryDocument with:
     type=purchase_receipt, status=draft, store, currency,
     exchangeRateToBase, purchase link and document date.
  3. It adds one IN line per remaining receivable PurchaseEntry:
     remaining = quantity - receivedQuantity.
  4. It copies product, warehouse, remaining quantity, unit cost snapshots
     and purchaseEntry link onto each line.
  5. It sets line totals and document totals from the receipt quantities.
  6. Added PurchaseController::receive() with CSRF protection.
  7. Added a purchase show-card Receive button for
     ordered/partially_received purchases with receivable lines.
  8. The action creates a draft and redirects to the inventory document,
     where the existing Post action performs the stock-changing receipt.
  9. Added service and controller tests.

  Dependencies:
  - Purchase, PurchaseEntry mappings and snapshots.
  - InventoryDocument and InventoryDocumentLine mappings.
  - InventoryPostingService validation:
    purchase_receipt requires IN lines.
  - DocumentProgressRecalculator and BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer
    for received/partially_received status.
  - Existing admin purchase reload-card behavior.
end note

note right of [12.6.2 Order shipment UI action]
  Goal:
  Make order ready_to_ship/partially_shipped -> shipped executable
  from the order UI.

  Implemented:
  1. Added OrderShipmentUseCase in the business/service layer.
  2. It builds a draft InventoryDocument with:
     type=sale_shipment, status=draft, store, currency,
     exchangeRateToBase, order link and document date.
  3. It adds one OUT line per remaining shippable OrderEntry:
     remaining = quantity - canceledQuantity - shippedQuantity.
  4. It copies product, warehouse, remaining quantity, price snapshots
     and orderEntry link onto each line.
  5. It sets line totals proportionally from the order entry total.
  6. OUT movement cost still comes from InventoryPostingService and
     WarehouseStock.averageCost during posting.
  7. Added OrderController::ship() with CSRF protection.
  8. Added an order show-card Ship button for
     ready_to_ship/partially_shipped orders with shippable lines.
  9. The action creates a draft and redirects to the inventory document,
     where the existing Post action performs the stock-changing shipment.
  10. Added service and controller tests.

  Dependencies:
  - Order, OrderEntry mappings and snapshots.
  - StockReservationService completion during sale_shipment posting.
  - InventoryPostingService validation:
    sale_shipment requires OUT lines.
  - DocumentProgressRecalculator and BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer
    for partially_shipped/shipped status.
  - Existing admin order reload-card behavior.
end note

note right of [12.6.3 Immediate order readiness sync after confirm]
  Goal:
  Avoid a UI dead end after confirming an order.

  Implemented:
  1. OrderManager::confirm() now reserves stock and immediately calls
     BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer::syncOrder().
  2. The synchronizer remains the source of truth for derived
     awaiting_stock/ready_to_ship statuses.
  3. The sync records status changes with transition=sync_progress via
     OrderHistoryRecorder.
  4. Readiness calculation counts active stock reservations belonging to
     the same order entry as available for that order, so the order's own
     reservation does not make it look out of stock.
  5. return_to_draft remains available from confirmed, awaiting_stock and
     ready_to_ship before shipment.
  6. Added tests for:
     confirmed order with enough stock becomes ready_to_ship;
     confirmed order without enough stock becomes awaiting_stock;
     partial backorder reservation becomes awaiting_stock;
     draft/canceled/delivered/completed are not overwritten.

  Dependencies:
  - OrderManager.
  - BusinessDocumentStatusSynchronizer.
  - OrderHistoryRecorder status sync history.
  - WarehouseStockRepository and StockReservationService behavior.
end note

note right of [12.6.4 Linked inventory document navigation and audit tests]
  Goal:
  Make the full cycle testable and understandable from UI.

  Implemented:
  1. Order show card displays linked inventory documents with compact
     links to the inventory document index focused by id.
  2. Purchase show card displays linked inventory documents with compact
     links to the inventory document index focused by id.
  3. Inventory document show card keeps links back to the linked order
     or purchase.
  4. Controller tests cover the receipt and shipment action buttons,
     invalid CSRF tokens, linked document navigation and redirects.
  5. Use-case tests cover draft document creation and remaining
     quantity calculation.
  6. Integration-style controller tests cover:
     purchase ordered -> received -> completed;
     order ready_to_ship -> shipped -> delivered -> completed.

  Dependencies:
  - Existing InventoryDocumentController show/post/cancel actions.
  - Existing quick-action JSON keys: card, history, row.
  - Status history for order, purchase and inventory documents.
end note

note bottom
  Verification for implementation:

  - docker compose exec php php bin/console lint:container
  - docker compose exec php php bin/console lint:twig templates
  - docker compose exec php vendor/bin/phpunit tests/Manager tests/Service tests/Controller
  - docker compose exec php php bin/console doctrine:schema:validate --skip-sync

  If JavaScript or SCSS is changed:
  - docker compose exec php yarn encore dev
end note

@enduml
